[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69742,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Skene gland adenocarcinoma is a malignant tumour arising in female urethral accessory glands.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69743,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8140/3 Carcinoma of Skene glands</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69744,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C93.0 &amp; XH22Z8 Adenocarcinoma of urethra or paraurethral gland &amp; Carcinoma of Skene, Cowper, and Littr&eacute; glands</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69745,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> urethral accessory gland adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69746,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69747,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are localized mainly in the distal urethra and arise from Skene glands, which are homologous to the male prostate. The presence of a tumoural mass in the anterior vaginal wall and bladder neck have been also documented {7507278; 32795117; 29901570}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69748,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients may present with gross haematuria or urinary urgency, or they may be asymptomatic. Serum PSA level may be elevated {29901570}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69749,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Skene gland adenocarcinoma is an extremely rare tumour. It occurs in women, mostly those in menopause, with patient age ranging from 46&nbsp;to 91&nbsp;years {29901570; 28872768; 32795117; 9584326; 28730423}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69750,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69751,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mutation and loss of heterozygosity of the <em>PTEN</em> gene have been detected in one case {32795117}. No further information is available.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69752,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Skene gland adenocarcinomas are flat to polypoid tumours measuring 10&ndash;35&nbsp;mm in the largest dimension {7729746; 14668555; 29901570; 32795117}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69753,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Overall architecture and cytological features are very similar to those of acinar prostatic adenocarcinomas. Tumours are arranged in a tubular or cribriform pattern (with pseudostratification in the latter), although solid areas, a single-file pattern, and even intestinal-like morphology have been documented. Neoplastic cells are positive for classic prostatic markers like PSA, PAP, and NKX3-1, as well as for AMACR and P501S {23018210; 29901570; 7507278; 28872768; 32795117}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69754,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69755,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69756,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a tumour with acinar to cribriform architecture and usually columnar epithelium; tumour morphology almost identical to that of prostatic acinar adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> a positive reaction with prostatic immunohistochemical markers (e.g. PSA, NKX3-1).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69757,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The eighth-edition American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) and Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM system can be applied.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69758,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 228,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Very few cases have been reported. One case has metastasized to inguinal nodes {9584326}. Cases with increased PSA serum level and with decreased PSA after surgical excision of the lesion, can then be followed up by the serum level of PSA {20870432; 7525428; 31883942}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]